(:id "rust/W16" :state :unknown :note "the emitted runtime has no conjoined second guard lane: a nested union's arm entries take the INNER union's tag offset as their only guard (fixedruntime.go's union case calls compile_entry with `their_at, j as u64 + 1, their_tag as u8`), so an arm inside an arm does not answer to the OUTER tag; docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.9 row 6 names the conjoined lane as the follow-on and it is not in this tree")
(:id "rust/R28" :state :unknown :note "the runtime stores one inline (guard, arg, argw) per TableFixedEntry and walks `for p in plan`; there is no pool of (guard, arg, argw) links addressed by offset+count and no chain to bound, so docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.2's partition/pool shape is not implemented on this leg and nothing can assert it")
(:id "rust/W6" :state :unknown :note "the read loop tests each entry's guard inline (`if p.guard != TABLE_FIXED_NO_GUARD`); there is no `split` index with every unguarded entry before every guarded one, so docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §4.2/§5.2's plan partition is absent on this leg")
(:id "rust/P1" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/rusttable/fixedroadmap_t08_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapRustT08WritesConformance/rust/P1") :tested-revision "6602f33eb")
(:id "rust/W13" :state :unknown :note "layout+hash == the C++ reference needs the generated corpus (build/fixedform-corpus/manifest.txt) and a cargo run to compare bytes; this tree has no build/ corpus (make tables-fixedform-corpus needs the C++ reference) and no cargo, so the assertion can neither run nor bite here")
(:id "rust/P2" :state :unknown :note "write-read-write byte-identical needs the emitted code to RUN; no cargo is on this machine and no sibling serialize.rs is checked out, so the round trip cannot be executed here")
(:id "rust/R27" :state :unknown :note "the manifest is the wire needs build/fixedform-corpus/manifest.txt; the corpus is not generated in this tree and the C++ reference that writes it is not built, so there is no oracle file to read")
(:id "rust/P3" :state :unknown :note "hostile bytes sweep + sanitizer needs the emitted code to RUN over forged files; no cargo on this machine and no corpus, so the sweep cannot be executed here")
(:id "rust/P4" :state :unknown :note "wrong plan goes red is a negative control that runs the emitted reader with a deliberately wrong plan; no cargo on this machine, so the control cannot be built or watched")
